quran[14]{c,v,t}:
  67,13,"And whether you speak in secret or aloud, certainly He knows best (even) the things (hidden) in the hearts."
  67,14,"Does He, Who has created, not know? In truth, He is the One Who can see the essence and is Well Aware (of everything)."
  67,15,"He is the One Who has made the earth soft and subservient to you. So walk about through its tracks and eat of the sustenance (given) by Him, and towards Him alone is the return, rising (after death)."
  67,16,Have you gone fearless of (the Lord of) the heaven that He may sink you into the earth when it suddenly shakes?
  67,17,Have you gone fearless of (the Lord of) the heaven that He may send against you a stone-pelting wind? Then soon will you come to know how My Warning is!
  67,18,"And surely, those before them (also) denied. But how (awful) proved My denial!"
  67,19,"Have they not seen the birds above them spreading out their wings and (sometimes) folding them? Nothing can hold them (from falling) except (the law made by) the Most Kind (Lord). Surely, He sees everything best."
  67,20,"Well, is there anyone that can muster an army to help you against the Most Kind Lord? The disbelievers are merely (snared) in deception."
  67,21,"Well, is there anyone that can provide you sustenance if (Allah) holds back His sustenance (from you)? In fact, they are adamantly fixed in rebellion and hatred (for truth)."
  67,22,"Is he who walks in prone position more rightly guided, or he who walks upright on a straight path?"
  67,23,Say: ‘(Allah) is He Who created you and provided you with ears and eyes and hearts. Yet you give thanks but little.’
  67,24,"Say: ‘He is the One Who has spread you in the earth, and you will be gathered towards Him (on the Day of Assembly).’"
  67,25,And they say: ‘When will this promise (of the Day of Resurrection) be fulfilled if you are truthful?’
  67,26,"Say: ‘The knowledge (of that Hour) is with Allah alone and I am just a clear Warner.’ (If the time is disclosed, there will be no fear any more.)"
